  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Top small-business government contractors ranking lists the largest small-business recipients of federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Total obligations for the set equal $25.2B. ATLANTIC DIVING SUPPLY, INC. leads the list with $3.8B in obligations. CSI AVIATION, INC received $1.3B, W S DARLEY & CO received $1.2B, MINBURN TECHNOLOGY GROUP, LLC received $927M, and AMERICAN CENTRIFUGE OPERATING, LLC received $916M. GENERAL MATTER, INC. received $900M, V3GATE, LLC received $862M, THUNDERCAT TECHNOLOGY, LLC received $856M, FOUR POINTS TECHNOLOGY, L.L.C. received $804M, and FCN, INC. received $654M. The list shows which small businesses captured the most federal contract obligations so far in the fiscal year. All figures are contract obligations, and current-year totals are partial because the numbers reflect the fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who tops the FY2026 to date list of small-business federal contractors?",
        "body": "ATLANTIC DIVING SUPPLY, INC. is the top small-business contractor by obligations with $3.8B. CSI AVIATION, INC follows with $1.3B and W S DARLEY & CO follows with $1.2B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What does the total $25.2B represent?",
        "body": "The $25.2B figure represents total contract obligations for the ranked small businesses in FY2026 to date. The note clarifies that these are obligations and that current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is ongoing."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Who is the largest small-business federal contractor in FY2026?",
      "a": "ATLANTIC DIVING SUPPLY, INC. is the largest small-business federal contractor in FY2026 to date. ATLANTIC DIVING SUPPLY, INC. received $3.8B in contract obligations during FY2026 to date."
    },
    {
      "q": "How are these small-business contractor rankings calculated?",
      "a": "Rankings are calculated by total contract obligations during FY2026 to date. All figures are contract obligations, and current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is to date."
